// t_80dad2dd: a declared half colour output whose value passes through a
// TEMP that the allocator places in R0.
//
// H0 is the low half of R0, so this is the shape a blanket "no temp in R0"
// guard refused - 45 of the reference SDK's fragment programs, this one
// among them (CgTutorial/GCM/HDR/shaders/OneHalfFp.cg is the same source).
// It is not a conflict: the temp's LAST READ is the instruction that writes
// the colour, so ordinary liveness separates them, and the reference emits
// exactly that overlap - `TEXR R0.xyz, f[TEX0], TEX0` then
// `MOVH H0.xyz, R0`.
//
// What keeps a temp that is still live off the slot is the allocator's
// output reservation (outputStorePos), not a guard in the emitter.
sampler2D gTexture;

half4 main(float2 texCoord0 : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR
{
	half4 c = tex2D(gTexture, texCoord0);
	c.a = 1.0;
	return c;
}
